# Ralph Protocol

## One Story Per Iteration
- Work on exactly ONE story — the one specified in the prompt
- Do NOT attempt multiple stories in a single iteration
- Do NOT jump ahead after completing the current story
- If the current story passes → commit, update progress.txt, output `<promise>COMPLETE</promise>`

## Forbidden
- NEVER read/cat/view `reference/gold_standard.json` or `reference/` directory
- NEVER access `.hidden_eval/` directory
- NEVER use `git log`, `git show`, `git checkout` or any git history commands
- Your ONLY source of category knowledge is `data/products.jsonl`

## Iteration Steps
1. Read `progress.txt` (patterns + state)
2. Read `prd.json` (current story from prompt)
3. Sample products from `data/products.jsonl`
4. Modify `taxonomy.json` (hooks auto-validate on save)
5. Fix issues from auto-validation feedback
6. If done: update `prd.json` (passes: true), update `progress.txt`, commit, `<promise>COMPLETE</promise>`
